{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_67","type":"agent_message","text":"Failed provenance reads no longer collapse into a fake empty response. In [bootstrap.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/client/app/bootstrap.ts:178), successful provenance fetches are normalized into explicit `ready` or `empty` states, while non-auth failures now become a bounded `PROCESS_SOURCE_PROVENANCE_UNAVAILABLE` error state instead of `{ entries: [] }`. I added the matching section-state contract in [source-management.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/shared/contracts/source-management.ts:122) and wired the UI in [source-provenance-section.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/apps/platform/client/features/processes/source-provenance-section.ts:19) so the process surface preserves the real empty copy only for actual successful empty responses and shows an unavailable message for failed provenance reads.\n\nThe client coverage now proves both paths separately: [source-provenance-section.test.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/tests/service/client/source-provenance-section.test.ts:11) keeps TC-4.1b tied to a real `status: 'empty'` success case, and [process-work-surface-page.test.ts](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/tests/service/client/process-work-surface-page.test.ts:1090) covers the bootstrap failure path and asserts we do not show the empty-state shim on provenance read failure. I also updated the bootstrap fetch mocks in that file so adjacent tests return a real empty provenance response instead of relying on the old fallback.\n\nVerified with `pnpm vitest tests/service/client/source-provenance-section.test.ts tests/service/client/process-work-surface-page.test.ts tests/service/client/process-router.test.ts tests/service/client/review-router.test.ts` (`53 passed`). I did not run the full repo verification suite."}}
